{
  "id": "profile-app",
  "title": "Tastebuds: add an entry, then give it credit",
  "formats": [
    "16:9"
  ],
  "voice": "kokoro:bm_george",
  "captionStyle": "plain",
  "stage": "plain",
  "systems": {
    "app": {
      "repo": "..",
      "baseUrl": "http://localhost:4173",
      "build": "npm run build",
      "serve": "npm run preview"
    }
  },
  "scenes": [
    {
      "type": "card",
      "template": "title",
      "fields": {
        "kicker": "Tastebuds",
        "title": "Add an entry, then give it credit",
        "subtitle": "The profile app, start to finish",
        "mark": ""
      },
      "beats": [
        {
          "say": "Tastebuds keeps a taste profile. This is how you add an entry, and how you move it once it shapes your work."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "browser",
      "system": "app",
      "start": "/",
      "beats": [
        {
          "say": "The app runs in your browser. A profile is one file on your disk, so there is no account."
        },
        {
          "say": "Open the example. It is the profile of Rosa, a home cook.",
          "do": [
            {
              "click": "text=See the example",
              "at": "example"
            },
            {
              "waitFor": ".columns"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "say": "A profile keeps two lists apart. Inspirations gave something to her cooking, and she credits each one. Taste references are cooks whose taste she watches.",
          "label": "two lists, *kept apart*"
        },
        {
          "say": "Add a taste reference: a bakery she likes.",
          "do": [
            {
              "click": ".relation.tasteReference header button",
              "at": "Add"
            },
            {
              "waitFor": "dialog[open]"
            }
          ],
          "label": ""
        },
        {
          "say": "Give it a name, a kind, and a link to its own site.",
          "do": [
            {
              "type": "dialog [name=name]",
              "text": "Sol Bakery",
              "at": "name"
            },
            {
              "select": "dialog [name=kind]",
              "value": "studio",
              "at": "kind"
            },
            {
              "type": "dialog [name=sameAs]",
              "text": "https://solbakery.example/",
              "delay": 25,
              "at": "link"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "say": "Tags say what you see in it.",
          "do": [
            {
              "type": "dialog [name=tags]",
              "text": "butter, morning buns",
              "at": "Tags"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "say": "Save, and it joins the taste you watch.",
          "do": [
            {
              "click": "dialog button.primary",
              "at": "Save"
            },
            {
              "waitFor": ".card[data-id=sol-bakery]"
            },
            {
              "scroll": ".card[data-id=sol-bakery]"
            },
            {
              "zoom": ".card[data-id=sol-bakery]",
              "scale": 1.7
            }
          ],
          "label": "a _taste reference_: nothing taken yet"
        },
        {
          "say": "Months later, your cookbook borrows the way it folds butter into its morning buns. Now it has shaped your work.",
          "hold": 1200,
          "label": "then it *shapes* her work"
        },
        {
          "say": "So move it to inspirations.",
          "do": [
            {
              "click": ".card[data-id=sol-bakery] .move",
              "at": "move"
            },
            {
              "waitFor": "dialog[open]"
            }
          ],
          "label": ""
        },
        {
          "say": "The app asks two things: what it gave, and which work of yours credits it.",
          "do": [
            {
              "type": "dialog [name=gave]",
              "text": "The three-fold butter method in the morning buns.",
              "delay": 30,
              "at": "gave"
            },
            {
              "type": "dialog [name=creditedIn]",
              "text": "Sunday Table, a cookbook",
              "delay": 30,
              "at": "credits"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "say": "Save. The entry moves across, with its credit beside it.",
          "do": [
            {
              "click": "dialog button.primary",
              "at": "Save"
            },
            {
              "waitFor": ".relation.inspiration .card[data-id=sol-bakery]"
            },
            {
              "scroll": ".relation.inspiration .card[data-id=sol-bakery]"
            },
            {
              "zoom": ".relation.inspiration .card[data-id=sol-bakery]",
              "scale": 1.7
            }
          ],
          "label": "an *inspiration*: credited by name",
          "hold": 2500
        },
        {
          "say": "A taste reference never shows as an influence. An inspiration always names what it gave.",
          "label": ""
        },
        {
          "say": "Then save the file, or export it for a web page.",
          "do": [
            {
              "unzoom": true
            },
            {
              "scroll": -4000
            },
            {
              "zoom": ".bar button.primary",
              "scale": 1.5,
              "at": "save"
            }
          ],
          "hold": 2000
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "card",
      "template": "title",
      "fields": {
        "kicker": "Tastebuds",
        "title": "Credit where it is due",
        "subtitle": "Open source. One file. No account.",
        "mark": ""
      },
      "beats": [
        {
          "say": "Tastebuds is open source. The guide has the rest."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
